We also have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed, and their contact information is available at dpo@nexus-engineering.it. Our GDPR posture includes a data protection impact assessment (DPIA) capability, which we can use to assess the potential risks associated with our solution and implement necessary mitigations.

In terms of technical security controls, we enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and we have experience with role-based access control (RBAC) design. Our network security architecture is based on zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth patterns, and we have intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDS/IPS) deployed.

To ensure the integrity of our logs, we use an append-only method with SHA-256 hash chaining, and we retain audit logs for 7 years. We also have a security incident response team (SIRT) in place, which can respond to security incidents and notify relevant parties within the required breach notification delay of 72 hours.

Overall, by leveraging our existing security controls and compliance measures, we can ensure that our solution meets the required GDPR regulations and provides the necessary explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued.
