2026-05-27 15:11:19,853 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: Based on our company context, we propose a solution that leverages our expertise in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities. We can deploy a sovereign model like Mistral 7B Instruct, which has strong French-language performance and is self-hostable, to provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents.

To facilitate access to information and improve answer quality, we can utilize our RAG capabilities, including dense vector retrieval and semantic chunking strategies. Our experience with vector stores such as Qdrant and Weaviate will enable us to efficiently manage and retrieve relevant information from existing systems.

To reduce processing times, we can optimize the model's performance using quantization methods like INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ), which have been shown to reduce energy consumption while maintaining comparable task performance. Our average accuracy gain from fine-tuning is around 12%, which can be achieved through LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on domain-specific corpora.

To integrate with existing systems, we will focus on developing APIs and interfaces that allow seamless interaction between our solution and the municipal agents' work environment. Our experience with system integration and technical constraints will ensure a smooth deployment process.

Regarding explicability of recommendations, we can employ explainability methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME to provide transparent and trustworthy outputs. Our EU AI Act limited risk compliance and bias testing process will guarantee that our solution meets regulatory requirements.

However, we are aware of known trade-offs, including the explicability vs. performance trade-off, where sovereign open-weight models like Mistral 7B may achieve lower relevance scores (~84%) compared to larger proprietary models (~92%). Additionally, online learning from user data is prohibited due to GDPR constraints, and we will rely on offline quarterly fine-tuning on anonymized data instead.

Overall, our proposed solution combines the strengths of LLMs, RAG, and explainability methods to provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents while addressing technical, regulatory, and environmental constraints.
