Another trade-off involves the choice between on-premise servers and green energy, as described in our "on_premise_vs_green_energy" CSR tension. In such cases, we recommend that clients subscribe to renewable energy Guarantee of Origin certificates to ensure their electricity comes from sustainable sources.

Lastly, the performance of larger models versus smaller, more energy-efficient ones is a consideration, as outlined in our "performance_vs_model_size" CSR tension. We typically prefer quantised mid-size models with fine-tuning over large unoptimised models to balance performance and environmental impact.

By implementing these sustainability measures and being mindful of potential trade-offs, we believe Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can help the City of Belval achieve its goal of reducing the environmental footprint of its systems of information while maintaining high performance standards.
