2026-05-27 15:15:57,087 | AGENT | Final proposal generated: # 1. Executive Summary
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks. Our solution leverages large language models (LLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, and explainability methods to provide intelligent assistance while addressing technical, regulatory, and environmental constraints.

# 2. Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval seeks an AI-powered solution that facilitates access to information, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and integrates with existing systems while ensuring high availability, security, and compliance with GDPR regulations. The project has a total budget of €3 million over four years and aims for minimal environmental impact.

# 3. Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes the Mistral 7B Instruct model, a sovereign French-language LLM that can be self-hosted to ensure data sovereignty. For RAG capabilities, we will employ dense vector retrieval using Qdrant or Weaviate as our vector store, enabling efficient management and retrieval of relevant information from existing systems.

To meet the response time requirement of less than 2 seconds, we will leverage Cloud architecture expertise using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for containerization and scalability. Our experience with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack ensures optimal system performance.

For integration, we will use API standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP to integrate with business software (civil status, town planning), electronic management of documents (EDM) systems like Alfresco or OpenKM, and user directories. We have experience hosting on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, specifically with Outscale and OVHcloud.

To ensure explicability and transparency, we will implement explainability methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME. Our solution complies with GDPR regulations through ISO 27001 certification, anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio, and a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed.

Our budget is aligned with the project's total value of €3 million over four years. While we cannot provide a specific projected margin without additional information, our target gross margin percentage is 28%, and our minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18%.

To reduce environmental impact, we partner with green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, utilizing 100% renewable energy and implementing digital sobriety techniques such as model quantization (INT8/INT4), auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy.

# 4. Unaddressed Requirements
No specific requirements mentioned in the tender are left unaddressed by our proposal, given the information provided by the agents. However, ongoing monitoring of updates to the AI Act and other relevant regulations is necessary to ensure compliance throughout the project's duration.

# 5. Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its consortium partners, offers a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval's needs for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. Our proposal integrates technical expertise in AI/ML, security and compliance measures, cost-effective solutions, and sustainability practices to provide a robust and environmentally conscious system. We are confident that our approach will enhance the efficiency of municipal services while respecting all regulatory and environmental requirements.
